# Integer Money Rules

## Rate card (YAML → Postgres seed)

| cargo_type | vehicle_type | rate_per_km | stop_fee |
|------------|--------------|-------------|----------|
| general | trailer | 12_000 | 500_000 |
| general | single | 10_000 | 400_000 |
| refrigerated | trailer | 15_000 | 600_000 |

Seed one commission rule: name `"default"`, `commission_rate_bps = 1000` (10%), active.

## Calculation (integer math only)

```python
base = distance_km * rate_per_km + stop_fee * max(0, stop_count - 1)
gross = base
commission = round(gross * commission_rate_bps / 10_000)
driver_net = gross - commission
assert driver_net + commission == gross
```

## Quote caching

- `force_recalculate: false` — same shipment + same inputs → return existing quote (same `quote_id`)
- `force_recalculate: true` — bump `quote_version` (1, 2, 3…)

## Response fields

Include `breakdown`: `base_amount`, `distance_amount`, `stop_fee`, `rate_per_km`, `commission_rate_bps`. Currency always `"IRR"`.
